# {{.Module}}

Requires Go 1.26 or 1.27. No Docker or C compiler required.

```sh
hyrule service create products
go mod tidy
go run .
```

Open http://localhost:8080/api/docs (default PORT is 8080).

```sh
curl -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"name":"Master Sword"}' localhost:8080/products
curl localhost:8080/products
```

SQLite persists to `hyrule.db`; set `SQLITE_PATH` to change it. Authentication
is disabled for local experimentation when no configuration source is supplied.
The generated program listens on loopback by default. Configure authentication
before setting `LISTEN_HOST` to expose the API.
SQLite is experimental: no outbox, dry run, soft delete or advanced queries.
See https://gui-rondon.github.io/hyrule/docs/reference/sqlite for limitations.
Use Mongo or Postgres for the existing production-oriented backend paths.
